<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Official privacy policy for the BataiBato mobile application (package: com.bataibato.app) and website. Covers personal data handling, location services, safety, and data deletion."
  lastUpdated="November 2026"
  lang="en"
>
  <p>
    BataiBato ("we", "our", or "us") is dedicated to protecting the privacy and personal data of our users, riders, and driver partners. This Privacy Policy outlines our transparent practices regarding data collection, GPS tracking, security safeguards, and account management for the BataiBato mobile application (package: <strong>com.bataibato.app</strong>) and website.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
  <p>
    To facilitate safe, dependable community ride sharing across Sindhuli and Nepal, we collect the following categories of information:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Personal Identification Details:</strong> Full name, verified mobile phone number, and email address provided during account registration.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Precise Geolocation Data (GPS):</strong> Real time foreground and background location data are collected when the application is active or during an ongoing trip to match nearby drivers, navigate accurate routes, calculate distance, and monitor rider safety.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Driver Partner Verification Records:</strong> Government issued driving licenses, vehicle blue books (ownership documents), license plate numbers, and vehicle inspection photographs.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Commute and Transaction History:</strong> Detailed trip records including pickup coordinates, destination points, timestamps, distance traveled, and digital payment receipts.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical Device Information:</strong> Smartphone model, operating system version, network carrier, IP address, and anonymized performance crash logs.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. Purpose of Processing and Usage</h2>
  <p>
    Collected data is processed strictly for legitimate operational purposes:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Connecting commuters with nearby verified drivers through intelligent proximity matching.</li>
    <li>Calculating transparent, distance calibrated fares in Nepalese Rupees (NPR).</li>
    <li>Providing real time GPS monitoring and shareable emergency tracking links.</li>
    <li>Facilitating digital payments through verified gateways including eSewa, Khalti, and mobile banking.</li>
    <li>Ensuring full compliance with the transportation regulations of Nepal.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Third Party Disclosures and Data Sharing</h2>
  <p>
    We never sell, rent, or trade your personal data to external advertisers. Data sharing is limited strictly to necessary service operations:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Between Commuters and Drivers:</strong> Upon ride acceptance, only your first name, pickup location, and vehicle plate number are visible to your travel partner.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Infrastructure Partners:</strong> Mapping providers (Google Maps API), SMS gateway providers, and verified digital wallets (eSewa, Khalti).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Legal Compliance:</strong> Authorized government authorities or law enforcement agencies when strictly mandated by the legal statutes of Nepal.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Data Retention and Account Deletion Procedures</h2>
  <p>
    In compliance with Google Play Store guidelines and international data protection standards, users have the absolute right to request account and data deletion at any time.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>How to initiate deletion:</strong>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Open the BataiBato mobile app, navigate to <em>Settings &gt; Privacy &gt; Delete Account</em>, and confirm your request.</li>
    <li>Or, send an email to <strong>support@bataibato.com</strong> with the subject "Account Deletion Request" from your registered contact.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Upon verification, all personal identifiers, trip histories, and associated records will be permanently purged from our active databases within 48 hours.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Children’s Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    BataiBato services are strictly directed to individuals aged 16 and above. We do not knowingly solicit or collect data from minors without parental supervision.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Data Security and Infrastructure</h2>
  <p>
    All sensitive transmissions are protected using end to end industry standard encryption (TLS/SSL). Database access is restricted behind multi factor internal access controls.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Contact and Inquiries</h2>
  <p>
    For inquiries or data privacy requests, contact our compliance officer:
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>BataiBato Privacy Desk</strong><br />
    Kamalamai Municipality, Sindhulimadhi, Bagmati Province, Nepal<br />
    Email: <strong>support@bataibato.com</strong><br />
    Website: <a href="https://bataibato.github.io/en/">https://bataibato.github.io/en/</a>
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
